From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xnix Maintainers <maintainers@xnix.local>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 20:36:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] package/wine: allow host-wine PE tools on aarch64

Wine 10 requires PE cross-compilation support when configuring host-wine
on an aarch64 build host. Buildroot's host-wine cut-down option set
unconditionally disables MinGW/PE tooling, which prevents Wine from
using clang, lld, and llvm-dlltool in the Xnix Colima builder.

Keep the target Wine package lean, but allow host-wine to detect the
available PE toolchain.
---
 package/wine/wine.mk | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/package/wine/wine.mk b/package/wine/wine.mk
index 1111111111..2222222222 100644
--- a/package/wine/wine.mk
+++ b/package/wine/wine.mk
@@ -285,9 +285,8 @@ HOST_WINE_CONF_OPTS += \
 	--without-gphoto \
 	--without-gnutls \
 	--without-gssapi \
 	--without-gstreamer \
 	--without-krb5 \
-	--without-mingw \
 	--without-netapi \
 	--without-opencl \
 	--without-opengl \
-- 
2.39.5
